menu "LBR CAN bus"

    config LBR_CAN_TX_GPIO
        int "TWAI TX GPIO (to transceiver TXD)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            GPIO driving the CAN transceiver TXD pin. -1 means not configured:
            pins are TBD until the node schematic is confirmed (issue #15),
            and the node refuses to start CAN while this is -1.

    config LBR_CAN_RX_GPIO
        int "TWAI RX GPIO (from transceiver RXD)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            GPIO reading the CAN transceiver RXD pin. -1 means not configured.

    config LBR_CAN_BITRATE
        int "CAN bit rate (bit/s)"
        default 500000
        help
            Shared bus bit rate; every node must use the same value.
            DAQ-WIRING.md starts at 500 kbit/s (robust on a vibrating, noisy
            car) and moves to 1 Mbit/s only if the measured bus load is too
            high. The system CAN budget in docs/can-ids.md is computed at
            this rate (about 42 % planned, ceiling 50 %).

    config LBR_CAN_RX_QUEUE_LEN
        int "RX queue length (frames)"
        default 256

    config LBR_CAN_TX_QUEUE_LEN
        int "TX queue length (frames)"
        range 8 127
        default 64
        help
            Must hold a node's worst-case burst: every slot, the heartbeat,
            and the 12 health pages can come due at the same instant, and
            the IMU Controller may forward all four corners' batches at once
            (it sets 127; checked for every plan in
            dev/tests/host/test_plans.c).

endmenu
